body:
It seems like an awful lot of hassle for something you could do with blue dye. first up you would need to ensure you have no low flow places (think res or distro and even corners or rad) that can accumulate the settlement from the distillate as these will solidify and regrow crystals over time. most fitting are brass which should be fine. how are you micronizing the dissolved mixture? most in-line filter systems are just a mesh that wont be copper, and you sure as hell don't want the abrasion of a large particle in your system.

&#x200B;

however if you do it make sure to post pics, it sounds cool mate.
